{"authored" [{"question" "q-161516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/9d6a1a5ca848d7563763a3384855daf13031c808852efa541a73e2ef3126c6ed.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}4xy\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above. \n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161516/review.json" "file_sha256" "6e851729af4d3b5f92b6a90253f7fe14e66a2b8c54a89d9acd70ad3a2f02b296" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161516/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "2c481768d52780b27f641d38fdb237714625a9c6a400eaa5e551ec9b9eeabea9" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161516/verification.json" "basis" 2023 "rationale" "Correct only the isolated dropped factor y in the intermediate integrand12xy−4x²y+4xy². The diagram is the unit-square base with topz=3−x+y and its integral4xy gives3. Preserve prompt, diagram, source, all existing fields, answer identities, and correct key."} {"question" "q-161516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/35113579a0c74805710c8787ba8738cd76c2777d59cf2a0cd234b284760ca6f6.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3-x+y},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/012a2a575147df3cf7fc0a5b85443d461c77c8447797969d8b96d9007cbfffd2.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3-x+y}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4xy\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x+y}4xy\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x+y}4xy\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-x+y}4xy\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[4xyz]_{z=0}^{z=3-x+y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4xy(3-x+y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(12xy-4{x}^{2}y+4x{y}^{2})\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(12xy-4{x}^{2}y+4x{y}^{2})\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(12xy-4{x}^{2}y+4x{y}^{2})\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[6x{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6x-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x)-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{22}{3}x-2{x}^{2})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{22}{3}x-2{x}^{2})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{11}{3}{x}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{11}{3}-\\frac{2}{3})-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161516/review.json" "file_sha256" "6e851729af4d3b5f92b6a90253f7fe14e66a2b8c54a89d9acd70ad3a2f02b296" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161516/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "2c481768d52780b27f641d38fdb237714625a9c6a400eaa5e551ec9b9eeabea9" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161516/verification.json" "basis" 2023 "rationale" "Correct only the isolated dropped factor y in the intermediate integrand12xy−4x²y+4xy². The diagram is the unit-square base with topz=3−x+y and its integral4xy gives3. Preserve prompt, diagram, source, all existing fields, answer identities, and correct key."} {"question" "q-161516" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161516/review.json" "file_sha256" "6e851729af4d3b5f92b6a90253f7fe14e66a2b8c54a89d9acd70ad3a2f02b296" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161516/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "2c481768d52780b27f641d38fdb237714625a9c6a400eaa5e551ec9b9eeabea9" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161516/verification.json" "basis" 2023 "rationale" "Correct only the isolated dropped factor y in the intermediate integrand12xy−4x²y+4xy². The diagram is the unit-square base with topz=3−x+y and its integral4xy gives3. Preserve prompt, diagram, source, all existing fields, answer identities, and correct key."} {"question" "q-161516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/9d6a1a5ca848d7563763a3384855daf13031c808852efa541a73e2ef3126c6ed.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}4xy\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above. \n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/